(M1 test A: one 2Sigma+ state with constant spin-rotation gamma: Hund's case (b).)
(The M1 operator g_s S cannot change N, so the parity-allowed line)
(J=0.5,N=0 -> J=1.5,N=2 must vanish. F1-F2 spin-flip lines inside one N)
(have the analytic strength g_s^2 (2J+1)(2J'+1) {S J' N; J S 1}^2 S(S+1)(2S+1).)
masses 1.0 16.0
molecule fictitious
nstates 1
jrot 0.5 - 3.5
symmetry Cs(M)
grid
  npoints 151
  range  0.55 2.0
  type 0
end
contraction
  vib
  vmax 4
end
poten 1
name "X2Sigma+"
type polynomial
lambda 0
mult 2
symmetry +
units cm-1
values
c0     0.0
re     0.97
c1     0.0
c2 40000.0
end
spin-rotation 1 1
name "<X|SR|X>"
lambda 0 0
spin 0.5 0.5
type polynomial
values
c0 0.5
end
intensity
  magdipole
  absorption
  thresh_intes 1e-300
  thresh_line 1e-300
  temperature 300
  gns 1.0 1.0
  J, 0.5, 3.5
  freq-window 0.001, 50000
  energy low -0.001, 50000, upper -0.001, 50000
end
